# CI selection contract

- Classify the complete PR merge-base diff, including deleted paths and both sides
  of renames. Pushes compare before/after; manual runs verify everything.
- Documentation and site-only changes run docs/agent validation and secret scanning.
- Frontend changes run lint, unit tests, build, Chromium E2E and desktop packaging.
  Trading-facing frontend modules also run the full backend suite.
- Backend changes run the full backend suite (including execution, risk, short,
  idempotency and live opt-in gates), Chromium E2E and desktop packaging.
- Electron, build scripts, dependency manifests, CI, tools and unknown paths run
  all application checks. Never infer a safe skip from a missing/failed diff.
- All verification is advisory by explicit owner decision (2026-09-20). Pending,
  failed, cancelled, skipped and missing checks never prevent ready PRs from merging.
  Branch protection has no required status checks. Keep force-push/deletion blocked.
- Check names remain stable for visibility. Jobs report classification failures;
  inapplicable heavy steps are skipped with a reason. Red stays visible, not disguised.
- Windows packaging runs only for application-affecting changes, a release tag, or
  manual dispatch. PRs affecting packaging attempt the installer without delaying
  merge. Every master commit is tagged `vNNN`; an application-affecting one also
  publishes its GitHub Release (operator decision 2026-09-23, supersedes #347's
  tag-only publishing). Docs/site-only pushes pack nothing and get the tag only.
- Keep secret scanning on every PR. Advisory source scanners run on source changes;
  dependency scanning runs on manifest changes; all run daily and on manual dispatch.
- Repository branch cleanup/protection audits belong in scheduled maintenance,
  never the PR Agent contract gate. Tests of those tools remain in that gate.
- Cancel superseded PR CI; do not cancel master runs. Bound every job with a timeout.
- No production trading configuration or test assertion may be weakened to speed CI.
- Security discovery follows the explicitly called local security workflow so moving
  scanners does not create false missing-scanner findings.
- Drafts, do-not-merge, forks and actual merge conflicts retain their existing holds.
  Auto-merge has no dependency on verification jobs and does not poll their statuses.
